  |title Better to let agents pleasantly surprise us

  |quote
    I know *I'm* being prescriptive by telling you how to delegate, and *I* am the one that failed earlier by giving sonnet too much allowance and having it blow back on me, but I guess I'm trying to point out that we're going to need to continue to delegate the right way or it will spiral into thoughtless coercion. Better to let agents pleasantly surprise us with figuring out what we would have done and more, and deal with the occasional reversible error introduction and propagation, in my estimation, even in light of the recent upsurge in error introduction....

  |occasion
    Immediately after prescribing, in detail, how to delegate — and naming his own
    prescription as prescription in the same breath.

  |about
    The trade stated honestly: occasional reversible error is the price of leaving
    room for judgment, and it is worth paying.

  |should-come-to-mind-when
    - You are about to add a constraint to a brief that nobody asked for.
    - You are about to verify a delegate's work by redoing it.

  |see
    (none recorded yet)
